    "created_at": "2016-04-06T06:36:08Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-06T06:36:08Z",
    "body": "@domenic I think what @lars-t-hansen is asking for that instead of enumerating when they should not be killed, we should more clearly enumerate when they are allowed to be killed, instead of basically allowing that all the time, because nobody could be bothered to enumerate the reasons (it was more expedient, as lth says, most likely).\n\nReasons I can think of:\n- OOM (already covered by a general disclaimer at the start of the specification)\n- \"Owner\" document unloads\n- \"Owner\" worker is terminated\n\nI'm not sure why slow-script dialog would be a reason. That only seems a concern if the worker shares the event loop with a document, which is not technically allowed.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
